    <name>🌿 LIVE CHLOROPHYLL / ALGAL ACTIVITY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<h2>LIVE CHLOROPHYLL / ALGAL ACTIVITY</h2><p><b>Data time:</b> 2026-09-23 08:00 AM EDT (newest of 7-day mosaic)<br/><b>Source updated:</b> n/a (ERDDAP)<br/><b>Source version:</b> nesdisVHNnoaaSNPPnoaa20NRTchlaGapfilledDaily-v3-2026-09-23<br/><b>Processed:</b> 2026-09-25 09:29 AM EDT<br/><b>Status:</b> LATEST AVAILABLE (daily composite)</p><p><b>Legend</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/chlorophyll/legend.png?v=nesdisVHNnoaaSNPPnoaa20NRTchlaGapfilledDaily-v3-2026-09-23" width="600" alt="legend"><br>Chlorophyll-a concentration (mg/m^3), logarithmic (base-10) scale: <b>LOWEST 0.079</b> (dark blue) → common 1.23 (green/yellow) → <b>HIGHEST+ 99.93</b> (deep purple). Equal color per decade of concentration (ocean-color standard); displayed values are true concentrations, never altered. High values indicate biomass/activity, not toxins.</p><p><b>Source:</b> NOAA CoastWatch S-NPP+NOAA-20 VIIRS chlorophyll-a NRT gapfilled Daily (ERDDAP nesdisVHNnoaaSNPPnoaa20NRTchlaGapfilledDaily), fallback SQ Daily (nesdisVHNSQchlaDaily)<br/><a href="https://coastwatch.pfeg.noaa.gov/erddap/griddap/nesdisVHNnoaaSNPPnoaa20NRTchlaGapfilledDaily.html">https://coastwatch.pfeg.noaa.gov/erddap/griddap/nesdisVHNnoaaSNPPnoaa20NRTchlaGapfilledDaily.html</a></p><p>Transparent outside valid water data so existing project layers (shipwrecks, lighthouses, harbors, parks) stay visible. Turn on/off independently of all other layers.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p>]]></description>
    <Folder>
      <name>LIVE CHLOROPHYLL / ALGAL ACTIVITY</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<h2>LIVE CHLOROPHYLL / ALGAL ACTIVITY</h2><p>Chlorophyll-a concentration at the lake surface, a proxy for phytoplankton abundance/biomass. NOT a toxin measurement and NOT a harmful-algal-bloom diagnosis.</p><p><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/chlorophyll/legend.png?v=nesdisVHNnoaaSNPPnoaa20NRTchlaGapfilledDaily-v3-2026-09-23" width="600" alt="key"></p><p>Chlorophyll-a concentration (mg/m^3), logarithmic (base-10) scale: <b>LOWEST 0.079</b> (dark blue) → common 1.23 (green/yellow) → <b>HIGHEST+ 99.93</b> (deep purple). Equal color per decade of concentration (ocean-color standard); displayed values are true concentrations, never altered. High values indicate biomass/activity, not toxins.</p><p><b>Units:</b> mg/m^3<br/><b>Source:</b> NOAA CoastWatch S-NPP+NOAA-20 VIIRS chlorophyll-a NRT gapfilled Daily (ERDDAP nesdisVHNnoaaSNPPnoaa20NRTchlaGapfilledDaily), fallback SQ Daily (nesdisVHNSQchlaDaily)<br/><b>Update:</b> daily composites<br/><b>Data time:</b> 2026-09-23 08:00 AM EDT (mosaic 2026-09-23..2026-09-17)<br/><b>Processed:</b> 2026-09-25 09:29 AM EDT<br/><b>Why high values turn red/purple:</b> Very high values (blooms, algal activity, turbid intrusions) compress into red-violet/deep-purple; common background concentrations own most of the color resolution.<br/><b>Provenance:</b> <a href="https://coastwatch.pfeg.noaa.gov/erddap/griddap/nesdisVHNnoaaSNPPnoaa20NRTchlaGapfilledDaily.html">ERDDAP dataset</a></p>]]></description>
